  "description": "Explore key concepts of artificial intelligence (AI) algorithms and programming for robot systems. Build a mental framework for AI in robotics; examine reactive sensing–acting loops; and design, implement, and evaluate autonomous systems and human–robot interaction. Consider machine learning and ethics; survey robotics fundamentals; and work with the basic components of robot systems. Practice robotics programming, computer vision, motion planning, mobile mechanisms, and manipulator kinematics. Engage with sensing, actuators, control theory, robot coordinate systems, differential motions, path control, dynamics, force control, and robot simulation. Investigate automation and robot programming languages; integrate actuators and sensors throughout.",
